# Memory

## Project
- **Calquary** — broad multi-category calculator/reference site (like CalcBE.com / calculator.net), positioned as a "reference library" not a generic SaaS tool.
- **Stack**: Plain HTML/CSS/JS, zero dependencies, no framework, no package.json (by choice — keep dependency-free).
- **Key files**:
  - `js/calculators-data.js` — single source of truth: CATEGORIES + CALCULATORS arrays (id, category, title, keyword, description, intro, fields, compute(), faq, related)
  - `js/engine.js` — shared rendering engine, renders any calculator's form/results from its config
  - `css/styles.css` — bespoke design system: Paper/Ink/Brand(forest green)/Accent(ochre)/Muted/Line palette, Fraunces + Inter + IBM Plex Mono, card-catalog concept
  - `build.js` — Node script (uses `vm` to load the browser-global data file), generates `tool/*.html` + `category/*.html` from `_templates/*.html`, plus `sitemap.xml`
  - `_templates/tool.template.html`, `_templates/category.template.html`
- **Categories** (call-number codes): M Math, F Finance, C Construction & Home, H Health & Fitness, D Date & Time, V Everyday Conversions, T Text & Digital, P Pet & Lifestyle
- **Current content**: 57 calculators live. Construction & Home complete at 12/12. Finance at 10/11 (retirement-calculator deferred). Health & Fitness at 10/11 (pregnancy-due-date deferred). Everyday Conversions complete at 10/10. Date & Time complete at 8/8 (timezone-converter, countdown-timer, anniversary-calculator excluded — live-data dependency or too close to existing tools). Other categories (Math, Text, Pets) still at 2 each — next candidates for the same keyword-research-first workflow.
- **Date parsing gotcha**: `new Date("YYYY-MM-DD")` parses as UTC midnight, then `.getDay()`/local getters can read back a different calendar day depending on the browser's timezone (classic off-by-one bug). Fixed in day-of-week-calculator and week-number-calculator by splitting the date string into y/m/d integers and using local (`new Date(y, m-1, d)`) or explicit UTC (`Date.UTC(y, m-1, d)`) construction instead of re-parsing the ISO string. Not retroactively fixed in earlier date tools (days-until, age, date-duration, business-days) since their outputs are differences where the error tends to cancel out — worth revisiting if it ever surfaces as a real bug report.
- **Select field gotcha**: `type: "select"` options must be `{v, l}` objects (value/label), NOT plain strings — engine.js reads `opt.v`/`opt.l`. Caught and fixed when first added to bmr/calorie/body-fat calculators (no prior select-field example existed in the codebase to copy from; checkbox-group already used this shape).
- **Dev loop**: `node build.js` then `npx serve` for local preview (localhost:4173)
- **Git**: initialized, 2 commits (site scaffold; Claudify toolkit install)

## Priorities
- SEO is an **active priority** — lean on `.claude/skills/seo/` (keyword-clustering, technical-seo-audit, schema-markup-generator, internal-linking-strategy, etc.) as calculators are added, not just opportunistically.
- Near-term goal: **add more calculators** to fill out thin categories, following the existing fields/compute/faq/related pattern in `calculators-data.js`, then `node build.js` after each batch.
- Keep the site dependency-free — no package.json unless the user asks.
- Preserve the current visual design system in `css/styles.css` — ask before structural changes.

